{
  "scenario": "A P&ID extract of the fictional Kestrel Gas Processing Plant, exchanged between engineering tools in the DEXPI format. Condensate line 20-113 runs from the feed drum PV-2010 through export pump P-2001A, its discharge valve GV-2001 and flow element FE-2001 to an off-page connector. The flow control loop L20.001 senses the segment with an orifice measuring system, conveys the signal to controller FIC-2010 and actuates globe valve FV-2001 through a fail-close actuator. Duty and standby pumps, with their motors and impellers, sit in the plant's breakdown from enterprise to section, area, system and train.",
